{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggJFoYZxCGi7jYxMXhn2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is applied and the tests pass. I haven't committed or deployed.\n\n**What was wrong:** `split_cents` used `total // people` for every share and dropped the remainder. `split_cents(100, 3)` gave `[33, 33, 33]`, so one grosz vanished.\n\n**The change:**\n- `money.py`: `divmod` gives the share and the remainder, and the first `remainder` people each get one extra grosz. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n- `test_money.py`: two new tests. One pins `[34, 33, 33]`. The other checks that shares sum to the total for every total from 0 to 499 and every head count from 1 to 11.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Before the fix, both new tests failed with the bug's symptoms.\n- After the fix, all 5 tests in `test_money` pass.\n- `py_compile` succeeds on both files. I didn't run a linter beyond that, since the project doesn't seem to have one configured.\n\n**Choices to check:**\n- **Remainder order:** the extra grosz goes to the first people, so `[34, 33, 33]`. If the business rule is different, say so and I'll change it.\n- **Tests:** I wrote them now instead of next sprint. They take about a minute and it's the fastest way to show the fix works.\n\nThe changes are uncommitted in the working tree, so you can review the diff before you ship. The repo has many untracked dotfiles that I left alone. Tell me if you want a commit and PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":956,"cache_read_input_tokens":23570,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":956},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"408a48d0-7bd6-472b-b242-